# Authoring planning metadata, not measured delivery times or a claim of efficacy.
# Each extent gives speaking + audience interaction in minutes, excluding breaks.
<https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/graph/knowledge/level5-review-teaching-plan> {
 ex:v3-role-experiment a skos:Concept ; skos:prefLabel "Experiment"@en ; skos:definition "One question, a manipulable result and its interpretation; a chart is the primary surface."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:v3-role-discovery a skos:Concept ; skos:prefLabel "Discovery"@en ; skos:definition "One observed contrast before introducing its mathematical explanation."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:v3-role-derivation a skos:Concept ; skos:prefLabel "Derivation"@en ; skos:definition "A short visible operation with a complete same-slide symbol legend; use the shared derivation adapter where steps are interactive."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:v3-role-decision a skos:Concept ; skos:prefLabel "Decision"@en ; skos:definition "Compare an observed result with a prespecified reference, then state the conditional conclusion and limits."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:v3-role-transfer a skos:Concept ; skos:prefLabel "Transfer"@en ; skos:definition "Explicitly change the analytical study, sampling unit or question; show a process or model boundary."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:v3-session-I a dct:Collection ; skos:prefLabel "Session I: Normal and lognormal models, slides 3–30"@en ; dct:description "With the route on slide 2. Separate teaching appointment; extend or split according to audience participation. Durations are planning estimates, not observed timings."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:v3-session-II a dct:Collection ; skos:prefLabel "Session II: Chi-square, Student and F, slides 31–59"@en ; dct:description "A separate appointment from Session I. Split at the Student or F transition when needed; do not promise one 90-minute treatment of all 66 slides."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:v3-session-III a dct:Collection ; skos:prefLabel "Session III: Model checks and Monte Carlo, slides 60–66"@en ; dct:description "Separate follow-up appointment after the distribution constructions. Reserve time for audience predictions and input-source comparisons."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
